\f1\fs22 The Elvi managed to fly under the radar of Moral Compliance until they spoke of the \'93One after the One\'94, the great leader to come, as the deliverer of hope. Moral Compliance cared not about silly songs righteously regaling the merits of saving trees and whales. \cb3 There were fuck-all trees and no whales left to save anyway. They could sing all they liked, it would amount to nothing. Prophesy was not something the company gave much credence, but the Elvi were preaching social change, equality and freedom. Giving hope to working class scum was something that would not be tolerated, the lows would not be permitted to taste of such rich fruit. The minority of the opulent must be protected from the majority. Radical and decisive action was needed to ensure they dined on ashes forever.\
